 # Sway idle and console locking
 
-On AC power, lock and blank after 30 minutes, then suspend after 60 minutes
-of total inactivity. On battery, lock, blank and suspend after 5 minutes.
+On AC power, lock and power down the monitors after 30 minutes, then suspend
+after 60 minutes of total inactivity. On battery, lock, power down the monitors
+and suspend after 5 minutes.
 The supervisor follows power-source changes and respects Sway idle inhibitors.
 The login remains on tty1; locking uses a separate Linux virtual console and
 authenticates with PAM. Both monitors mirror that console, so password entry
 is shared and only one successful authentication is required.
+
+## Idle monitor power-down — 2026-11-06
+
+The console locker now selects VESA power-down mode (`TIOCL_SETVESABLANK`,
+mode 3) for the explicit blank request instead of only clearing the picture.
+It resets the global mode to 0 immediately after that request, before waiting
+for a key. This keeps power-down from leaking into suspend or the return to
+Sway. A key wakes the monitors and opens the existing password prompt;
+authentication and the idle/suspend timeouts are unchanged.
+
+The kernel passes the selected mode to the console driver when blanking;
+changing the mode afterward does not itself unblank the console. See the
+[Linux VT implementation](https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/master/drivers/tty/vt/vt.c).
+Actual monitor power-down depends on the console driver's support. Failed
+mode-selection, blanking and reset ioctls are recorded in the journal.
 
